<title>USA: FOB Gulf Grain- Soy offers steady to lower.</title>
<headline>FOB Gulf Grain- Soy offers steady to lower.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. FOB Gulf soybean were steady to lower on Monday while corn values were mixed, dealers said.</p>
<p>Soft red winter and hard red winter wheat values were unchanged.</p>
<p>One dealer noted the continued volatility of the August/November spread on the Chicago Board of Trade behind the fluctuation of FOB soybean values.</p>
<p>He said the market was still eyeing the August CBOT soybean contract which expires on August 20.</p>
<p>On the export front, the Commodity Credit Corp was seeking up to 18,000 tonnes of U.S. hard red winter wheat and up to 22,000 tonnes U.S. corn for donation to Russia.</p>
<p>Both commodities were for September shipment.  </p>
